/-! # Kinnersley complex null frame on Kerr–Newman, Boyer–Lindquist (ATLAS-V-01)

B3 local layer (`mission/PHYSICS_BOUNDARY.md` §K; conventions `notes/ATLAS_V_SOURCE_DICTIONARY.md`). The metric is
IV's `KN.gKN M a Q` (signature `(-,+,+,+)`, coordinates `(t, r, θ, φ)`), used unchanged; nothing is re-derived.
With `Σ = r² + a²cos²θ`, `Δ = r² − 2Mr + a² + Q²`, `q = r + i a cosθ` (`qK`, Hintz's `ρ̄`), `q̄ = r − i a cosθ`:

    l = ((r²+a²)/Δ, 1, 0, a/Δ),           n = (r²+a², −Δ, 0, a)/(2Σ),
    m = (i a sinθ, 0, 1, i/sinθ)/(√2 q),   m̄ = (−i a sinθ, 0, 1, −i/sinθ)/(√2 q̄)

(contravariant components in the order `t, r, θ, φ`; the Kinnersley tetrad of Hintz arXiv:2609.33661v1 with the same
vectors). Frame index `A = 0, 1, 2, 3` ↔ `l, n, m, m̄`; `knT` has the frame vectors as **columns**.

Main results, on IV's regular set `domReg M a Q = {Σ ≠ 0, Δ ≠ 0, sinθ ≠ 0}` for every real `M a Q` (`a = 0`,
`Q = 0` allowed): all 16 complex-**bilinear** Gram entries (`gram`, matrix form `knTᵀ g knT = etaNull`), so in
signature `(-,+,+,+)` `g(l,n) = −1`, `g(m,m̄) = 1`, all other pairings `0`; `m̄ = conj m`, `l`, `n` real; the dual
coframe `knDual = etaNull knTᵀ g` is a two-sided inverse (`knDual_mul_knT`, `knT_mul_knDual`), the inverse metric is
`knT etaNull knTᵀ = giKN` (componentwise `g^{μν} = −l^μn^ν − n^μl^ν + m^μm̄^ν + m̄^μm^ν`) and `g = knDualᵀ etaNull knDual`;
every component is `C^∞` (order `∞`) on `domReg`. -/

